  "rule": "Legend strips hanging from the top row encode (colour c, height n). For each such strip, rank the bars standing on the bottom row whose cap colour is c by total height and repaint the n-th tallest one entirely in colour c; everything else is unchanged.",
  "scope": "Supports 8..20 rows x 9..26 columns, 1..4 legend colours placed adjacent or spaced apart at the top-left, legend heights (ranks) 1..3, n..n+2 (max 5) bars per colour with distinct heights 3..H-1, per-colour body colours disjoint from legend colours, bars in adjacent columns, and bars standing beneath a legend strip with at least one background cell of gap. Deliberately not supported: bars whose cap colour is absent from the legend, non-zero background, bars shorter than 3, and height ties within a colour group.",
  "constraints": [
    "Background is 0; legend strips occupy row 0 and run straight down with a single colour.",
    "Each legend colour appears exactly once in the legend and has at least n bars with that cap colour, so every legend instruction changes exactly one bar.",
    "Bar heights within a cap colour group are pairwise distinct (no ambiguous ranking).",
    "Every bar has height >= 3 so body cells exist and the fill is never an identity.",
    "Body colours are never a legend/cap colour and never background.",
    "Bars never reach row 0 (max height H-1); a bar sharing a column with a legend strip leaves >= 1 background cell between strip and bar so the column-wise scans stay separate.",
    "At most one bar per column; adjacency between bars is allowed because the rule is column-wise."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Legend strips are always placed starting at column 0 in the top-left, as in all fixtures; legends elsewhere along the top row are not sampled.",
    "Bars with cap colours not present in the legend (pure distractors) are not generated, since no fixture shows them.",
    "A deterministic fallback scene exists for the (practically unreachable) case where 200 sampling attempts fail."
  ],
